<br /> Centralia, PA.<br /> Basically, the town is on top of a coal fire that has been raging for 50 years. No one is allowed to move there but there are still residents that haven't moved out. This screams wyrm to me, although could easily be a demon or something equally terrible. Are the remaining inhabitants in the thrall of the wrym, or are they the defenders / guards keeping something truly horrific trapped.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned this in my Pentex media thread (under Harold and Harold Mining, IIRC), including the fact that it's probably the single best place in North America to put a Black Spiral Dancer hive. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-16T00:19:39-07:00","id":1260845,"title":"","content":"This is fun! <br /> <br /> Las Vegas Undercity. In the real world over 1k homeless are estimated to live in the city underneath Vegas, imagine in the World of Darkness. I\u2019m working on a 3rd city project we\u2019re there is an attempt to make the true inheritor to the 2nd City in an underground super catacomb under Vegas. With superghouled revanent pigs and rats and bugs for cattle, and fungi and imported ramen and preserved foods.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dubai Island. Man I would love a World of Darkness Dubai! The underwater Casino, and the artificial islands would be a great setting! Imagine living in the World Islands and having neighbors like the Manchester United team! It writes itself!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T09:49:30-07:00","id":1261312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>edd123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1259421-interesting-campaign-city-ideas#post1259421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I placed this in the general WoD section because it could easily be used for any of the games.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Centralia, PA.<br /> Basically, the town is on top of a coal fire that has been raging for 50 years. No one is allowed to move there but there are still residents that haven't moved out. This screams wyrm to me, although could easily be a demon or something equally terrible. Are the remaining inhabitants in the thrall of the wrym, or are they the defenders / guards keeping something truly horrific trapped.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.ranker.com/list/weird-american-small-towns/noah-henry\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://imgix.ranker.com/list_img_v2/5548/2425548/original/weird-american-small-towns-u1?w=1200&amp;h=675&amp;fm=pjpg&amp;q=80&amp;fit=crop&amp;dpr=1\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ranker.com/list/weird-american-small-towns/noah-henry\" target=\"_blank\"> The 20 Strangest Small Towns In The United States </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ranker.com/list/weird-american-small-towns/noah-henry\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.ranker.com/list/weird-american-small-towns/noah-henry </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Over 100K fans have voted on the 20 Strangest Small Towns In The United States. Current Top 3: Centralia, PA &ndash; On Fire Since The '60s, Whittier, AK &ndash; Everyone ... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I like the idea that Centralia is actually a fae freehold of some sort (coal fire, more like balefire!) who then ravage glamour from Instagram hipsters. Alternatively, it's not the wyrm that holds sway, but the weaver. Someone who refuses to move even after their town was on fire? Sounds pretty static.<br /> <br /> At this point though, the population is quite few, the fire is largely died down, and most of the buildings have been bulldozed, but that doesn't need to be the case in ones chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T16:54:02-07:00","id":1261664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1259421-interesting-campaign-city-ideas?p=1261312#post1261312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that Centralia is actually a fae freehold of some sort (coal fire, more like balefire!)</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd make an interesting location for a collection of Glomes and Solimonds.<br /> <br /> I've long wanted to set a Werewolf chronicle in the Everglades and surrounding areas.<br /> <br /> Added: I'd likely call it The River of Grass Protectorate, based around a long standing Uktena caern with a few other small ones scattered about, an even older Mokole nest, and two or three Pumonica den realms, as well as several clumps of assorted Kinfolk dominated small towns. Something that draws a lot on Carl Hiaasen's novels (and newspaper columns) and the classic 1970s Man-Thing from Marvel Comics.<br /> <br /> Really, southern Florida is a great place to set any of the main five games (as well as witch-hunters, Reckoning, and Demon).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 10-22-2018, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join